{"step_index":8480,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T21:36:23Z","thinking":"Initial review of the dropped matches reveals the potential for errors. The first item, `'بروتولوك40مجم اقراص س ج'` which was matched as `'کونترولوک ۴۰مجم اقراص'` in a previous process, shows a critical difference: \"Protiloc\" versus \"Controloc.\" It appears there is a clear mismatch in the core drug name, which needs further investigation to confirm why the match was dropped.\n\n\nThese initial mismatches represent incorrect brand substitutions, even if the active ingredients are the same, demonstrating that process PROC-014 correctly rejected the matches. Further review confirms this, with distinctions observed in brand names like \"Protiloc\" versus \"Controloc,\" \"Neocarbon\" versus \"Eucarbon,\" and outright drug type misclassifications, such as ampoules mistaken for tablets, and an active ingredient mismatch \"Gynozol\" versus \"Gynovazol\". Each of these observations justifies the rejection.\n\n\nFurther mismatches identified include \"U-Kerato\" versus \"Uricare\", indicating different products. \"Extra protein Vanilla\" versus \"Chocolate\" represents flavor discrepancies in nutritional products. While \"Bronchophone\" and \"Bronchof\" are both cough syrups, the different names indicate separate brands, another mismatch.\n\n\"Ciprocin\" versus \"Cipro\" are different brands, like the others, while \"Colmetidine\" (Cimetidine) versus \"Colmedine\" represent different medications. The final one is between the `Depakine Chrono 500mg` and what it was matched to is another difference. Each of these confirm previous assessments.\n\n\nExamining the rejected matches further, I find a critical distinction: the controlled-release formulation of valproate (Chrono) is not interchangeable with generic valproate (Debican) due to the epilepsy treatment. However, I have to re-evaluate items previously deemed valid in the prior process.\n\nI observe \"Neurovit\" with varying spellings (\"نيروفيت\" and \"نيوروفيت\"); these seem to be the same drug. The reason for the rejection of \"نيوروفيت\" is unknown. Similarly, \"Tryptizol 10 mg\" (تربتيزول / تريپتازول) appears as a perfect match despite being dropped. \"Neo-Carbon 30 tablets\" and \"Neo-Carbon capsules\" might also be valid matches.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Script to inspect all items added in PROC-014 that were not in PROC-012.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import openpyxl\n\nP12_PATH = r\"D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\data\\processes\\PROC-012\\results_PROC-012.xlsx\"\nP14_PATH = r\"D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\data\\processes\\PROC-014\\results_PROC-014.xlsx\"\n\ndef load_wh_matches(path):\n    wb = openpyxl.load_workbook(path, data_only=True)\n    wh_sheets = [s for s in wb.sheetnames if s not in ['ملخص', 'لم يُعثر عليه', 'يحتاج مراجعة']]\n    matches = {} # (wh_sheet, shortage) -> wh_item\n    for s in wh_sheets:\n        ws = wb[s]\n        rows = list(ws.iter_rows(values_only=True))\n        if len(rows) > 1:\n            for r in rows[1:]:\n                if any(r):\n                    shortage = str(r[0] or \"\").strip()\n                    wh_item = str(r[1] or \"\").strip()\n                    matches[(s, shortage)] = wh_item\n    return matches\n\ndef main():\n    m12 = load_wh_matches(P12_PATH)\n    m14 = load_wh_matches(P14_PATH)\n    \n    added_keys = set(m14.keys()) - set(m12.keys())\n    dropped_keys = set(m12.keys()) - set(m14.keys())\n    \n    print(f\"Total Added in P14: {len(added_keys)}\")\n    print(f\"Total Dropped in P14: {len(dropped_keys)}\")\n    \n    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n    print(\"ALL ADDED ITEMS IN PROC-014 (New matches found):\")\n    print(\"=\" * 80)\n    for wh, sh in sorted(added_keys):\n        print(f\"Warehouse: [{wh}]\")\n        print(f\"   Shortage: '{sh}'\")\n        print(f\"   P14 Match: '{m14[(wh, sh)]}'\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","Description":"Script to inspect all added items in PROC-014","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\kakak\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\scratch\\inspect_added_p14.py","toolAction":"Write inspect_added_p14.py","toolSummary":"Write script to inspect added items in P14"}}]}
